WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Let's make a moving cover for Stillform.

00:00:03.375 --> 00:00:07.150
Open the Stillform starter project.

00:00:07.208 --> 00:00:11.000
It already has fonts and cover components. Open Assets to add the photo.

00:00:11.083 --> 00:00:14.750
Click Import Files and choose the mountain photo.

00:00:14.792 --> 00:00:17.150
The photo now appears in your project assets.

00:00:17.208 --> 00:00:23.070
Tell Codex to use one photo, add the masthead, and bring it in almost immediately.

00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:25.650
Send the brief from the assistant panel.

00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:31.700
Codex builds the cover and checks the render. We have shortened the wait.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:39.150
Play the first cut. Notice how quickly the title arrives.

00:00:39.208 --> 00:00:42.650
Pause, choose Select Region, and box the title.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.990
Ask for the title to enter half a second later.

00:00:48.042 --> 00:00:53.280
Send the marked frame with your note.

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:59.400
Codex updates the entrance timing and checks the revised frames.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:06.900
Replay it. The photo now has time to breathe before the title arrives.

00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:12.890
Compare both openings. The revision is on the right.

00:01:12.958 --> 00:01:16.030
Choose Export MP4 and check the dimensions and frame rate.

00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:19.860
Choose a location and save the file.

00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:25.850
Studio renders on your computer. Wait for the export to finish.

00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:28.000
Here's the exported cover.

00:01:33.097 --> 00:01:39.067
Here is a second project, started from the kinetic type template. Open Motions and search for Clay World.

00:01:39.147 --> 00:01:44.867
Click the card to play its sample in the drawer. Add Only saves the motion in this project so you can use it later.

00:01:45.217 --> 00:01:56.217
Back in the editor, choose Assets, then Import Files. Pick your audio file. It appears alongside the other media in the project.

00:01:57.067 --> 00:02:06.717
Ask the assistant to use the sound as a quiet background track and keep your timing. Say when the clip should start and how long it should play.

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:13.667
In this prepared example, the timeline shows the sound under the scenes. Play the preview to check when it comes in.

00:02:16.117 --> 00:02:21.417
Export again to include the audio in your MP4.
